/* APEVERSE 2.1 - amsterdam_leidse.js : AMSTERDAM third district — Leidseplein nightlife (north bank of the Singelgracht, west of the
   Vijzelstraat).  world_amsterdam.js owns the ground, the canal and the bridges (the new Leidsebrug carries tram 2); this file builds
   the district as its own merged blocks and runs its life.  1 m = 1 m, north is -z.  Layout (not a survey of the real city):
     the Jordaan lane (x -197) runs south into the square; the Weteringschans quay runs along its south side; tram 2 comes over the
     Leidsebrug from the museum stop on the Stadhouderskade and ends in the middle of the square.
     Leidseplein: stone square, tram terminus, terraces, plane trees, giant street chess, a street performer's pitch, fietstaxi stand.
       north side: Grand Hotel De Leidse Hof (corner tower), Club Nachtegaal (walk-in club: dance floor, DJ booth, bar;
       open 22:00-05:00, wristband at the door), Bioscoop Lumen, Café De Zon.   east side: the Stadstheater (arcade, exterior).
     Korte Leidsedwarsstraat: the bar alley west of the square (projecting signs, string lights): Café Het Hoekje, Bar Vuurvlieg,
       Pizzeria Da Gino, Karaokebar De Zingende Aap, Shoarma De Nachtuil, Snackwand Kroket & Co (food from the wall),
       The Flying Dutchman pub, Hostel De Fietsbel; Het Lichthuis (concert hall in an old church, exterior) closes the end.
     Leidsebosje: a grove with benches between the theatre and the Vijzelstraat.
   Residents: Bram (doorman), Yara (DJ), Joris (street performer).  Every business is fictional.  Save: S.ams.lp (optional fields). */
